epic:#28130#1 · hotlong · session_040dfd80c4c9411b895c698e785a6848

Filing gate: ④ child of epic #28236 (P3, cut 2026-11-01 on the maintainer's 「四项提速措施全部按推荐执行」, schedule reviewed) · plan of record: ADR-0146 Rollout P3 "N-29 QA checklist and live e2e to the Studio door"; schedule review table: last, after N-28 and N-30. ⛔ Not a claim.

Blocked-by: #28578, #28577

Part of #28236 (P3, child **N-29**) · governs: ADR-0146 Consequences (checklist items and e2e specs that drive the Setup designer are "rewritten to the Studio door or marked transitional (N-29)"), the epic's two-minute check · lane: `domain:devx` (declared minor surface: one new spec in `ui/e2e/live/`) · size: L.

**Why it waits.** The checklist must describe what shipped. N-28 moves the last Setup → Metadata routes and Packaged automation, and N-30 settles the docs the items cite. Writing items earlier would pin URLs and copy that are about to change.

**Business reason.** The epic promises one behaviour a release tester can check in minutes:
- "customize" a HotCRM view, and three reads show the same columns;
- the export carries the declaration;
- "Restore package original" undoes it;
- a flow override runs only the new definition, and a waiting run finishes on the old one;
- a field added to a HotCRM object lands in `hotcrm.custom` as `xxx__c`;
- uninstalling HotCRM is refused, naming `hotcrm.custom`.

Today no checklist item and no live spec walks that journey.

**Measured (`35b178bd0a`).**
- 352 items over 16 areas (`docs/qa/platform-checklist/areas/*.json`). None covers the ADR-0146 `.custom` journey: a grep for `.custom`, `__c`, `ensure-customization` or `ADR-0146` hits only two unrelated custom-page items.
- 10 items name a Setup → Metadata route or Packaged automation:
  - api-backend: `packaged-action-disabled-dispatch`;
  - automation: `flow-node-type-matrix`, `packaged-flow-disable-durable`, `setup-packaged-automation-board`;
  - integration-system: `external-datasource-federated-read`, `external-schema-browser-ui`;
  - platform-core: `home-admin-cluster-links`;
  - studio-authoring: `object-designer-roundtrip`, `authoring-validation-not-persisted`;
  - ux-conventions: `write-feedback`.
- Overlay- or extension-shaped items to re-read: `studio-authoring.packaged-display-class-direct-edit`, `studio-authoring.org-override-registry-gate`, `studio-authoring.packaged-automation-studio-lock`, `platform-core.packaged-object-extend-only`.
- `studio-authoring.object-designer-roundtrip` already flags that its e2e (F2–F4) drives the Setup designer route, "a sibling door onto the same save".
- Validation is `pnpm check:platform-checklist` (README :11). The authoring procedure is the `checklist-author` skill.
- Live e2e: 21 specs in `ui/e2e/live/` (8 on the CI allowlist, `studio-object-designer` and `studio-editor` among them), CI allowlist `test:e2e:live:ci` (`ui/package.json:113`). Which showcase package serves as the read-only base for a journey: not verified.

**Wanted.**
1. Each of the 10 items, and each overlay- or extension-shaped item above, is re-measured against `main` after N-28. It is either rewritten to the Studio door (URL, steps, `automated.ref`) or marked transitional with the reason. Each change gets a `revisions` entry.
2. New items, one per promise, in their natural areas, citing the card that shipped each:
   - view, dashboard and report customize, export and restore (N-17);
   - flow override and "new similar" (N-11, N-18, N-22);
   - add field `__c` and the label patch (N-23c);
   - permission-set "new similar" (N-20b);
   - the ensure door and the pair uninstall refusal (N-13, N-14);
   - the `os migrate` ceremony (N-16a) and the closed package-less write (N-16b);
   - landing counts and directory marks (N-24, N-26b);
   - Setup → Metadata redirects, with datasource kept (N-28).
3. One live spec walks the journey through the Studio door on a read-only base: customize a view, check the served columns, restore it, add `region__c` and see it in the pair, try to uninstall the base and read the refusal. It joins the CI allowlist only if its runtime fits the job's budget. Otherwise it goes to nightly, and the PR says which.
4. `pnpm check:platform-checklist` is green, and `coverage.json` and `FOLLOW-UPS.md` are updated where the procedure requires.

**Tests.** `pnpm check:platform-checklist` exit 0. The new spec passes locally against showcase, with a failing-variant run attached: it must fail when one assertion is broken. One `checklist-test` run over the new items, recorded under `runs/`.

**Release safety.** Docs and tests only. No product code changes, so a release right after it ships the same product with a truthful checklist.

**Not here.** Moving routes (N-28). Skills and docs (N-30). Fixing a defect the run finds: each one gets its own card.

**Dedupe.** Searched `checklist custom package override` and `e2e studio customize view restore`. They return only #28236, #28509 (skills docs, N-30's first slice) and QA run records. #27377 is the release sweep, not this work.

